Algorithm: 

Step 1: Create a list to store all subsets of the given array.
Step 2: Start a recursive process with an empty subset and starting index 0.
Step 3: At each recursive call, add the current subset to the result list.
Step 4: Traverse the array from the current starting index to the end.
Step 5: For each element, include it in the current subset.
Step 6: Recursively continue the process with the next index to explore further subsets.
Step 7: After returning from recursion, remove the last added element to backtrack and explore other possibilities.
Step 8: Repeat this process until all possible subsets are generated.
Step 9: After the recursion completes, return the list containing all subsets.

Time Complexity: O(n × 2ⁿ)
Space Complexity: O(n) 


-----> Code <-----

class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> subsets(int[] nums) {
        List<List<Integer>> ans=new ArrayList<>();
        func(nums,ans,new ArrayList<>(),0);
        return ans;

    }
    public static void func(int []nums,List<List<Integer>> ans, List<Integer> al,int st){
        if(al.size()<=nums.length){
            ans.add(new ArrayList<>(al));
        }
        for(int i=st;i<nums.length;i++){
            al.add(nums[i]);
            func(nums,ans,al,i+1);
            al.remove(al.size()-1);
        }
    }
}
